WEBVTT

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:12.610
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.770
You're closing Gama Gama?

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.190
Why?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.090
That's the promise I made 
to the friend who built the aquarium.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.040
That I would close it 
if it got too old to sustain.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.240
Still, it's too soon!

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.160
It's better for the marine life, too.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.010
<b>No Closing!</b>

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.660
Kukuru...

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.030
<b>No Closing!</b>

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.780
I tried both the service entrance 
and the feed room.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.780
The entrance is no good, either.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.650
She blocked all the entrances.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:07.960
Amazing.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.950
Is this really the time to be amazed?

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.780
She's locking herself in because
she's unhappy. What is she, a kid?

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.200
I understand how Kukuru-chan feels, though.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.480
Kukuru, are you there?

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.260
Answer me if you're there!

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.100
Well, what can we do?

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.050
Why don't we take the day off?

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.950
The typhoon's coming, too.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.790
I don't think we'll have any guests.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.940
But...

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.770
Kai-kun, is the boat back at shore yet?

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:44.330
I don't think so.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.830
Fishers have it rough.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.140
Take care of your family today.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.360
Day off, huh?

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.880
Nice.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.890
Guess I'll clean my room.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:18.460
Food?

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.900
Just a second. I'll be done in a second.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.700
Okay, okay!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.520
Just this once.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.920
<b>Typhoon 13</b>

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.920
<b>Landing on Okinawa Island Tonight</b>

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:36.920
<i>A large and powerful storm, 
Typhoon 13 is approaching Okinawa Island.</i>

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.550
Thanks.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.500
It looks like it's headed here by nightfall.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.660
I wonder if she'll be home by then.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.660
I suppose she'll be staying the night.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.000
She has to care for the animals, too.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.050
Lunch is ready.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.270
Let's eat up.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:09.280
<i>I hope Kukuru isn't hungry and alone.</i>

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.790
<i>All alone.</i>

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.410
I—

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.920
Here, lunch boxes.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.300
Eat up.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.170
You all look well.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:07.930
What's wrong?

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.470
You aren't as ravenous.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.590
Maybe I'll switch up the food.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.430
I'll make some more.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.100
Kukuru, are you there? 
Open up!

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.200
Fuuka?!

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.860
Please! Let me in!

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.440
I won't!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.740
Kukuru!

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.040
Why did you come here?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.070
Are you here to tell me 
to stop being silly?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.060
No!

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.270
To convince me to come out?

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:32.990
No!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.400
To take me home, then?

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.020
No!

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:35.910
I...

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.830
I'm holing up with you!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.330
What?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:56.860
What do you even mean 
that you're holing up with me?

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.180
It means exactly what it means.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:01.080
I'm going to stay here with you.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:02.810
Why?

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.120
I never asked—

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:07.100
From Grams.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.740
You must be hungry.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.400
How much work have you gotten done?

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.700
Are you done feeding?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.250
I'm doing it now.

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:23.050
How about cleaning the prep table 
and sanitizing the knives?

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.010
Not yet!

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.000
I can do it myself!

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.010
Let me help.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.170
I never asked!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.260
Kukuru, I'm done cleaning.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:56.330
What?

00:07:56.650 --> 00:07:57.710
I'm done.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.350
What's next?

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.660
You can go home already!

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:02.960
I'll calibrate the pH meter then.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.380
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.930
Oh, man!

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.810
This one's going to be big!

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.600
I'm sorry. The tour will be canceled.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.940
We're asking that clients 
switch to another day or accept a refund.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.160
I'll call a taxi right now.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.710
Hurry up and get ready.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:58.550
What about you?

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.260
I'm staying.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.100
Then I'm staying, too.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:03.930
No!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.060
Go home, Fuuka!

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:08.690
I can't go home in this typhoon anymore!

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.960
This is something I'm doing myself.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.660
It's not your business.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.980
That's not...

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.290
It's your dream.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:30.420
Protecting Gama Gama is your dream.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.700
You asked me to help you with your dream.

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:38.300
I want to be helpful to you.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.940
I want to be by you.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:45.460
You'd just given up your dream back then.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.680
But not now.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.430
You're going to be in a movie.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.440
You're going back to 
being an idol, aren't you?

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.500
Not yet.

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.080
Just think about yourself, Fuuka.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:59.800
You don't need to help 
with my dream anymore.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:04.380
I'll see it through by myself.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.130
No.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.560
What?

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.700
I'm staying with you!

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:17.800
I said I'm fine!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:23.610
Oh, no...

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.160
An outage?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:29.060
<b>At the End of the Siege</b>

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:32.300
Huh?

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:33.630
It's the generator.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.030
It switches on automatically.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.900
I'll go make sure the tanks
are working properly.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:43.800
Me, too.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.630
Is there no power here?

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.690
The pumps and filters
are working, so it's fine.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.630
The lights are off at night, anyway.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.840
The fish have to sleep.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.640
We don't want their sleep cycles 
to get messed up.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.190
Huh.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.500
All good.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.240
The roof's leaking!

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.860
Crap! Bucket!

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.020
We just fixed the roof last year.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:35.960
I hope it's all right.

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:40.300
I never noticed, 
but this building's pretty old.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.550
Gramps said...

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:46.730
It's gotten too old 
to maintain the facility.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:51.160
But if it gets old and breaks down, 
we can always fix it.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.440
It'll still last if we take good care of it.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.780
Gama Gama is home to the sea life.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:59.440
They can't lose it.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:01.700
I'm going home!

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.120
And for me, too.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.720
I can feel Mom and Dad here.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:09.200
It's special to me.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:14.170
I was still small, 
so I don't remember much.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:18.170
My only memory of my family 
is at Gama Gama.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.810
It can't go away.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:23.210
No.

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:30.270
There.

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:33.780
There are typhoons in Okinawa every year.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.270
It's all right.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.910
We've overcome it every time.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.530
<b>Outage alerts</b>

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.530
<b>Outages are occurring all over Okinawa.</b>

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:49.110
Looks like they don't know 
when the power's coming back on yet.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:52.060
Normally they get it back right away.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.040
How long do the generators last?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.540
About seven hours.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:00.050
The power went out around ten, right?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:06.680
If it doesn't come back, the air pumps
and filters will stop, won't they?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.070
We won't be able to control 
the water temperatures, either.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.490
If that happens...

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:14.180
The sea life might not last half an hour.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.410
I'll contact Gramps!

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.310
No!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.230
It's too dangerous 
to go outside right now.

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:27.320
We're going to prepare for the worst.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.360
First, I'm going to get ready to save

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.960
the species that don't adapt well 
to changing water conditions.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.160
Come with me, Fuuka.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:34.970
Okay!

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.010
Make lots of bags of ice for cooling.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.040
Got it.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:49.180
I'll go get more tanks.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.690
Kukuru!

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.620
Give me something to hold it with!

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.510
Kukuru!

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.140
Use this!

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:52.490
Why?

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:56.900
We have to move the tanks!

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.320
Why?

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.250
Stop. Please.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:10.220
I only want to stay here.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.390
Kukuru!

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:19.590
Why can't I stay here?

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.810
Are you taking it away from me?

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:28.570
Like you did Mom and Dad?

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:32.020
You're taking what's precious to me?

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:35.000
I have nothing left!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.860
This place is all I have!

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:41.330
If I lose this place, I won't...!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.890
Kukuru!

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.410
This place isn't all you have!

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:58.800
It's not the end, even you lose this place!

00:15:58.800 --> 00:15:59.560
Never.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.220
Even if you lose your dream, 
you don't lose the future.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.150
We have to protect the animals' future.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:14.730
Yeah.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:16.370
Let's go.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.290
Hang in there.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.940
Please. Please...

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:36.720
Ack, what is this?

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.210
Watch your step.

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:40.180
Seriously?

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:43.050
Jesus, it's a haunted house.

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:43.600
Kukuru!

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:45.030
Kai.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:47.080
Are you hurt?

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:49.820
What about you, Miyazawa-san?

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:51.150
I'm all right.

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:52.860
Thank goodness.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:57.030
Umi-yan gave us a ride 
when the winds died down.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.600
The corals and anemones.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:03.380
Make sure the water temperature 
never rises above 25 Celsius.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.500
Roger.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.570
I split up the ice 
and put them in the freezer.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.420
You're well prepared.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.630
Take care of the moon jellies 
and community tanks.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.970
A'ight.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:17.900
Kai-kun, get the pipes 
ready for repairs.

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:18.780
Okay.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:22.680
The two of you, lid the deep
sea tanks with styrofoam.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.320
If the migrants don't look like 
they're getting enough air,

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:27.020
we'll use battery-powered pumps.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:27.980
Okay.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.700
Gramps, I...

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.050
Kukuru.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:21.910
Gramps.

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:24.800
Trust in the sea life.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:27.540
They aren't that weak.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:38.890
The power's back!

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:43.610
Restart the filters 
on Tank 12 and Tank 15.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.690
Watch out for air pockets.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:46.600
Okay!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:50.150
Let's bring the animals back home.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:24.180
You did well.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:26.940
Gramps...

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:30.010
You were right.

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:33.940
Gama Gama's at its end.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:38.540
We're going to put the animals 
in danger here.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.950
We can't protect it.

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:44.220
So...

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:52.840
They'll all be separated, but they'll
be just fine in their new aquariums.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.230
Yeah.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:57.750
Kukuru.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.830
Good work as acting director all this time.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:07.600
Thank you for protecting these kids.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.930
We're done bringing everything back online.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.030
I'm exhausted.

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.100
Um...

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.120
We're sorry for everything.

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:46.920
Sorry, Fuuka.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:50.650
I said lots of terrible things to you.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:55.060
I couldn't do it by myself.

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:59.030
If it weren't for you, 
I couldn't have protected the marine life.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.610
Thanks.

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:04.470
I'm the one who has to thank you.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.890
I thought I was doing it for you.

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:11.240
I wanted to be of use to you.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.510
I wanted to help you.

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:16.820
But that wasn't true.

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:20.010
It was all for myself.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:25.880
I never noticed that, by letting
me help you, you gave me strength.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:31.290
I don't think I hate working hard 
for someone else.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:41.030
We did everything we could, didn't we?

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:47.850
It's closing... isn't it?
